From 1684540bb9b5c74e2a3a519720db0a22af51cb73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hector Isaza <76170012+hecisaza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:16:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: a reply made only of DSML closing tags, with tools
 offered, is flagged (tool_parse_warning), not repaired

SvangenStudios's 0043 of the 4-Spark recipe (https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-4x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/pull/32),
ported. A reply whose whole answer is DSML closing tags (both spellings) and whitespace, with tools offered, gets
tensorfold.tool_parse_warning = "orphan_dsml_closers" in the whole reply, in a chat stream's finish chunk and in a
Responses stream's final response, and a log line with the reply id (Messages carries no tensorfold fields). Diagnostic only: content, token ids, usage and the finish reason are unchanged, no call is invented and no
retry started. output_diagnostics.zig is 0043's unchanged, plus a test-only switch; the check reads the same answer the
finish parses (after the think split, or the Harmony split thinking off), so it agrees with this engine's parse: such an
answer holds no opener, so the parse returns no call in either TENSORFOLD_TOOL_STREAM mode.

Tests: output_diagnostics.zig (0043's: the closers in both spellings, and prose, quotes, fences, JSON, an opener, a
spacing or a missing '>' not flagged) and dsml_stream_test.zig (the chat, Responses and Messages routes, live and hold,
whole and streamed in rounds of one byte and all bytes, thinking on and off, with and without tools, ended by the end
token or cut by max_tokens, and Harmony answers with thinking off: the warning only on chat and Responses for a
closers-only answer with tools, and every reply the same with and without the diagnostic once ids and times are set
aside).
